Supplement Table2 defines 223 reproducible hg19 eCLIP contexts (103 HepG2,120 K562); 203 have matched source RNA-seq experiments (92,111). Original supplement DESeq file IDs are no longer in the current publication metadata. Reconciled corrected Salmon/CQN GC-bias DESeq2 files by exact experiment and cell, preserving old IDs and control maps. Both original-control and batch-normalized representations exist. FUS/HepG2 has a control-ID conflict (Table2 ENCSR003EKR versus current metadata ENCSR491FOC); retain data but do not rank this contrast pending resolution. This is not an absent measurement.

Six pilot files were downloaded and checked against published MD5 and size, covering the first source-listed RBP in each cell and both DE representations. These native DE tables have a six-column header but a seventh row-name column; parse gene IDs explicitly. Paired files contain 20,474 rows, not the entire GENCODE gene universe; batch files have a smaller retained universe. PMP22 is explicitly ENSG00000109099.9, with hg19 minus-strand span [15133094,15168643), derived from the verified GENCODE19 GTF, not a guessed assembly or promoter interval. GTF annotation has eight PMP22 transcripts. The two pilot PMP22 baseMeans are 10.66 (HNRNPC/HepG2) and 29.37 (IGF2BP1/K562), with nonsignificant uncertain responses. Low expression is a live limitation, not enough to abandon the full eligible screen. These probe outcomes are exploratory and will not be presented as a pre-registered holdout.

Ranking specification before full screen: full source-defined paired contexts rather than preselected hits; require source credible IDR/input-enriched binding, positive measurable PMP22 counts with finite uncertainty, source all-gene FDR<=0.05 and across-PMP22-screen BH<=0.05, and documented adequate knockdown (at least50% loss in available source QC or measured target RNA with uncertainty). Use lower absolute 95% Wald effect bound and descriptive binding strength to order candidates; assess baseMean<20 as low-coverage sensitivity, not an imputed zero or a universal power cutoff. BY and batch-normalized analyses will be sensitivity checks, not independent replication. No hand-picked peak-positive denominator for multiplicity. Sites may nominate processing instead of decay. Strict thresholds are an explicit analytic choice informed by schema/pilot inspection, not a preregistered confirmation.

